! v1.10.3: CDFT release on a HETERO donor-acceptor pair (Delta /= 0):
! the Li ... ethylene ... F "harpooning" model on STO-3G (~4 min).
!
! The relaxed RKS Becke charge of Li is +0.250 (found by probing:
! a +0.25 constraint converges with V = 8.5e-4 Ha and the release
! stays put -- the equilibrium-detection trick).  This test prepares
! the partially harpooned diabat q_Li = +0.38 (0.13 e displaced),
! releases it, and the charge sloshes back through the pi bridge.
!
! ORACLES (companion Casida run: same geometry, %tddft 8 + dipmom):
!  * dominant beat of q_Li(t) = 0.06306 Ha vs the bright z-polarized
!    CT state 4 at 0.06427 Ha (f = 0.070, mu_tr,z = 1.279) -- the
!    -1.9 % offset is the amplitude-dependent mean-field shift
!    (0.126 e oscillation; the +0.25 probe run beats at 0.0653);
!  * oscillation amplitude 0.126 e (partial back-transfer: GMH gives
!    H_04 = 0.0114, Delta = 0.060 -> Rabi weight 4H^2/Omega^2 = 13%);
!  * t = 0 self-check 5.2e-11; released-run conservation 4.3e-9 Ha.
! GEOMETRY NOTE: at larger separations (Li 2.00 / F -2.30 A) the
! restricted reference has a SINGLET INSTABILITY (diradical
! Li*/F* character; Casida refuses with the (A-B) message) -- kept
! closer here so the closed-shell reference is stable.  A textbook
! lesson shipped as a test.
%method  PBE
%basis   sto-3g
%grid    1
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%scf_ptol 1e-6
%scf_maxiter 200
%cdft    becke
LiDonor  1  charge  +0.38
%cdft_tol 1.0e-6
%cdft_maxiter 25
%rt_tddft 1100
%rt_dt    0.2
%rt_gamma 0.015
%rt_pc_maxiter 4
%rt_print_every 500
%geom angstrom
Li   0.0000   0.0000   1.85
F    0.0000   0.0000  -2.00
C    0.6695   0.0000   0.00
C   -0.6695   0.0000   0.00
H    1.2321   0.9289   0.00
H    1.2321  -0.9289   0.00
H   -1.2321   0.9289   0.00
H   -1.2321  -0.9289   0.00
*end
